{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":40.7400016784668,"text":"A black stone, broken at the top, crowded with tiny writing, it is an announcement from 1960 B.C. about a boy king, Ptolemy V, written three times, in hieroglyphs for the priests, in everyday Egyptian for the people, and in Greek for the rulers, who were Greek at the time. French soldiers found it in 1799, inside an old wall in the town of Rashid, which Europeans called Rosetta. Because the Greek could be read, scholars finally had a key. Champollion turned it in 1822, and the hieroglyphs spoke again after 1,400 years of silence.","words":[{"word":"A","start":0,"end":0.5199999809265137},{"word":"black","start":0.5199999809265137,"end":0.8999999761581421},{"word":"stone","start":0.8999999761581421,"end":1.3600000143051147},{"word":"broken","start":1.9199999570846558,"end":2},{"word":"at","start":2,"end":2.2200000286102295},{"word":"the","start":2.2200000286102295,"end":2.6600000858306885},{"word":"top","start":2.6600000858306885,"end":2.740000009536743},{"word":"crowded","start":3.4800000190734863,"end":3.4800000190734863},{"word":"with","start":3.4800000190734863,"end":3.940000057220459},{"word":"tiny","start":3.940000057220459,"end":4.320000171661377},{"word":"writing","start":4.320000171661377,"end":4.699999809265137},{"word":"it","start":5.360000133514404,"end":5.5},{"word":"is","start":5.5,"end":5.639999866485596},{"word":"an","start":5.639999866485596,"end":5.860000133514404},{"word":"announcement","start":5.860000133514404,"end":6.179999828338623},{"word":"from","start":6.179999828338623,"end":6.599999904632568},{"word":"1960","start":6.840000152587891,"end":7.519999980926514},{"word":"B","start":7.519999980926514,"end":7.860000133514404},{"word":"C","start":7.860000133514404,"end":8.140000343322754},{"word":"about","start":8.600000381469727,"end":8.800000190734863},{"word":"a","start":8.800000190734863,"end":9.079999923706055},{"word":"boy","start":9.079999923706055,"end":9.30000019